Requirements for this to compile cleanly:

- **`Item` must be `Sendable`.** It crosses from the concurrent pool back to the main actor. A struct with `Sendable` members gets this inferred.
- **`Parser.parse` must be `nonisolated`.** Under main-actor default isolation, `Parser` is main-actor isolated unless you opt it out. Otherwise the compiler will report that calling it from `@concurrent` code needs `await` or isolation. Mark `Parser` as `nonisolated` (a type-level `nonisolated` applies to all members) if it is pure, and it will run off the main actor.
